reviewer.reply:
{
    "verdict": "reject",
    "blockers": [
        {
            "claim": "Session leak when bridge destroyed during async connect - the session is created, registered, and started in connectCoreOnly, but if the bridge is destroyed before the queued lambda runs, the session is leaked because there's no cleanup mechanism",
            "file": "app/qttunebridge.cpp",
            "quote": "const qttune_status_t rc = qttune_session_start(session);"
        },
        {
            "claim": "Session passed through lambda capture without ownership management - if the lambda is dropped, the captured session pointer is destroyed but the actual session is not freed",
            "file": "app/qttunebridge.cpp",
            "quote": "QMetaObject::invokeMethod(this, [this, uri, err, session]() {"
        },
        {
            "claim": "Destructor cleanup code removed without replacement - the original destructor had explicit cleanup for pending sessions, which is now gone",
            "file": "app/qttunebridge.cpp",
            "quote": "-    // A connect whose queued completion never ran (it was dropped with\n-    // `this`) left its session pending. It was never started, so no\n-    // worker is calling onFrame; destroy it like any other.\n-    if (qttune_session_t* pending = m_pendingSession.exchange(nullptr)) {\n-        qttune_session_destroy(pending);\n-    }"
        }
    ],
    "questions": [
        "Is the change to updateValues (only updating when subscribed is true) intentional? The original comment stated 'Values and history update regardless' but the new code only updates when subscribed",
        "How is the 'subscribed' field set and is it controlled by the Live checkbox as stated in the proposal?",
        "What does applyConnectedState do with the session - does it take ownership?",
        "How should tests verify the async connect behavior without the pendingSessionForTesting accessor?"
    ],
    "nits": [
        "The comment in the header for 'subscribed' was removed but should be updated to reflect the new behavior rather than just removed",
        "Consider using a guard object or RAII pattern for session lifetime management in the async path"
    ]
}
